    36	## 2. What the research changed
    37	
    38	The first research wave turned the projection from a nice-to-have into a requirement on both lanes.
    39	
    40	| Finding | Source | Consequence |
    41	| --- | --- | --- |
    42	| XTDB 2.2 indexes only `_id`. Other predicates are column scans at about 0.27 s per million rows. | R1 Q7 | The EAV ledger (`_id` = assertion id) turns entity and attribute lookups into full ledger scans. At 100m facts that is tens of seconds per query. Hot reads must resolve through `_id`. |
    43	| QLever's real reified layout is about 30 triples and 724 B per fact; with the journal, `54A + 27E + 63` triples per transaction. | R2, R4 | 3 to 5.7 billion triples at 100m facts, beyond the 60 GiB VM. A compact ledger (about 7 triples) plus a plain current graph (about 1.2) is about 0.8 billion triples and 17 GB. |
    44	| QLever updates cost O(total delta) per request and have no rollback. | R2 Q1 | Writes need one operation per request, a bounded delta with online `rebuild-index`, and roll-forward recovery. |
    45	| XTDB client-set system time is fragile: one abort moves the head to wall-clock. | R1 Q1 | Never set system time. Map commit positions to the system time the engine assigned (hypothesis H-X-CUT below). |
    46	| QLever string order is ICU; a 6-hex-digit-per-codepoint key sorts in codepoint order under the pinned engine, proven exhaustively. | R5 | The string-order blocker has a measured fix: +1 triple and about 58 B per text assertion. |
    47	| QLever EXISTS is planned uncorrelated; re-binding correlated variables inside the group fixes the counterexamples. | R5 | The correlation blocker has a verified authoring fix; planner memory per EXISTS must be costed. |
    48	| XTQL covers 11 of 71 native tasks today, all `state_at`. 57 tasks are SQL only. | R6 | XTQL parity is the largest single body of work in lane X. |
    49	| The XTDB native library has no task-wide fixed cut; XTDB snapshot tokens and fixed-basis read-only transactions work. | R6, R1 Q5 | Multi-call native tasks can pin one cut natively. |
