lab/research/R1-xtdb-capabilities.md:39:## Q1. Can a client set a transaction's system time over pgwire in 2.2.0?
lab/research/R1-xtdb-capabilities.md:41:**Verdict.** Yes. Four spellings work. The value must be strictly later than the latest completed transaction's system time, the resolution is one microsecond, and a violation aborts the transaction and moves the "latest completed" head forward. Mapping Triplex `recordedAt` onto native system time is possible only if nothing else ever writes to that database and every abort is accounted for.
