lab/research/R6-xtdb-gap-analysis.md:474:### Details
lab/research/R6-xtdb-gap-analysis.md:478:- Method: independent oracle replays events; capture P once; pause between capture and read, commit a second writer, resume at the captured P.
lab/research/R6-xtdb-gap-analysis.md:479:- Pass: retirement fields null before the retirement is known at (R, P); equal to oracle after; raw ordinary reads unchanged; XTQL and SQL agree row for row.
lab/research/R6-xtdb-gap-analysis.md:487:- Author XTQL for 04 relation_exists and coverage, 05, 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 12, 16, 17, 18 using `unify`, `join`, `aggregate`, `(not (exists? ...))`, `cast`. Keep the existing independent oracle and pins; new job identity (for example `xtdb-native-xtql-packet-v1`), separate from native142 so SQL results are not relabeled.
lab/research/R6-xtdb-gap-analysis.md:488:- Pass: 71 cases (current and reopen) match the oracle with a recorded trace language of XTQL for every call of these tasks.
lab/research/R6-xtdb-gap-analysis.md:501:- Load representative entities (10 facts each) at 10k, 100k, 1M entities through public writes. At each stage record data, log and buffer bytes after compaction, bytes per fact, and run point, selective filter, join, anti-join, aggregate, historical, interval, recursion and pagination families.
lab/research/R6-xtdb-gap-analysis.md:508:- On the experiment-7 100k fixture, compare identity lookup by `scope_key = ? AND id = ?` against `_id = '["scope","id"]'`, with `EXPLAIN ANALYZE`, for single and OR-chain forms (`scan.clj:167-180`). Check that results are equal under pending overlays and nested savepoints before using it in `retract`.
