lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:1:# R3: ORM prior art for Triplex over XTDB 2.2 and QLever 0.6
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:15:## 1. Answer first
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:17:### 1.1 Recommendation
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:21:1. **The canonical layer stays as it is.** XTDB keeps `tx_assertions`. QLever keeps assertion nodes in the per-scope graph. Triplex allows overlapping assertions for one entity and attribute and keeps two independent clocks per assertion. XTDB rows cannot hold that (XTDB enforces non-overlapping rectangles per `_id`) and the native-lane handoff forbids mapping `recordedAt` to XTDB system time without a proven cut mapping.
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:29:### 1.2 The layers
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:51:### 1.3 Decisions that need Sam
