lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:812:## 6. Pitfalls
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:816:| 1 | **N+1.** A lazy entity object (Datomic, Datascript) or one query per ref. | `include`, reverse include, `getMany` loops. | Level-batched `Triples.entities` first. XTDB `NEST_*`. QLever single CONSTRUCT. Cap include depth and use an id-only recursion guard as in Datomic pull. |
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:820:| 5 | **Null versus absent.** XTDB treats missing and `NULL` as one. SPARQL has unbound variables. LDkit uses `null` and `[]`. Datomic pull omits. Triplex has no null value. | Row contracts, patch semantics, JSON `null` inside a `json` attribute. | Documents omit absent properties. The row contract marks optional columns explicitly (`T.optional`). `null` is only a `patch` instruction. |
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:824:| 9 | **Numeric precision.** QLever inlines doubles with 60 bits. Integers beyond about ±2^59 are not native. `-0` and fractional milliseconds need exact channels. Node returns int8 as string or bigint. XTDB columns widen to unions. | Plain triples, `number` and `int64` attributes, instants. | Keep the `_order` and lexical channels as the exact path. State which plain-triple datatypes are exact (4.3.2). Decode `int64` through `hydrateNativeValue`. |
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:826:| 11 | **Tenant isolation.** XTDB: every tenant shares `tx_assertions`, isolated by `scope_key`. QLever: isolation is the scope graph. A bare `GRAPH ?a` reads other tenants' plain triples. | Direct psql or SPARQL console use. | Host-level boundary and, for QLever, one index per tenant when isolation matters. `FROM` injection does not work (4.3.5). |
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:828:| 13 | **Equating clocks.** Mapping Triplex recorded time to XTDB system time, or Triplex valid time to XTDB valid time, is not exact today. | Any native-temporal "optimization". | Keep Layer 1 on Triplex columns. Treat native-temporal projections as separate, gated work (4.2.5). |
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:834:## 7. Open questions and probes
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:841:| P2 | Does the `entity()` expansion in 4.2.4 return the same rows as the `facts()` oracle at several bases (before and after a correction, at a half-open boundary), and what does it cost at 1M assertions compared with `facts()`? Does `MAX ... FILTER` work on text and double columns? | Run both on the native-entry fixture, compare row sets. | Any row differs, or latency is more than a small multiple of `facts()`. |
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:842:| P3 | What does one named graph per assertion cost in QLever 0.6 (index build time, memory, `GRAPH ?a` joined to the scope graph) at 1M and 100M assertions? Is `INSERT { GRAPH ?g { ... } } WHERE { VALUES (?g ?s ?p ?o) { ... } }` accepted? | Synthetic load against the existing writer. | The update form is rejected, or build and query cost grow worse than linearly. |
lab/research/R3-orm-prior-art.md:843:| P4 | Is the implicit default graph the union of all graphs, and does `GRAPH ?g` bind the default graph as well? | Two small graphs, then a bare pattern and a `GRAPH ?g` pattern. | The source reading in 4.3.5 is wrong. |
