lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:81:| Via `entityType` on assertions | Yes, as a label only | `TripleInput.entityType` is optional (`packages/core/src/Triple.ts:8-16`). It lands in the indexed `entity_type` column (XTDB `codecs.ts:27`, QLever `rdf.ts:22`). Nothing validates it against a schema at write time. Validation is a separate pass (`EntityValidation.revalidate`). |
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:87:Design implication for thesis T1 (table-per-type projection): the writer needs the `EntityType` set at transaction time. The cheapest source is the in-process `EntityType` objects passed to the adapter factory, with the committed release checked against them by `cid` at startup.
