lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:151:### 2.3 CAS and preconditions
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:157:### 2.4 How Datalog reaches a backend
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:164:| QLever | `packages/qlever/src/QleverQueryExecutor.ts` (446 lines), `compiler.ts` (1013 lines), `recursion.ts` | Datalog AST to SPARQL over the reified graph. Includes optional "plan" profiles (aggregate, negation, source, retirement, scalar order) selected by constructor options (`QleverQueryOptions`). |
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:165:| KV (oracle) | `packages/core/src/kv/` | Hexastore scans plus nested-loop joins. `KvTriples.layer` is the in-memory reference runtime. |
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:167:Each backend's runtime is `Runtime.define({name, storage, queries})` (`packages/xtdb/src/index.ts:68`, `packages/qlever/src/index.ts:65`). `.layer({scope, capabilities})` binds a `DatabaseScope`. Scope is a JSON tuple `["triplex-scope-v1", env, tenant, database, generation]` (`packages/core/src/runtime/DatabaseScope.ts:22-29`), and `DatabaseScope.test(name)` builds a throwaway one.
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:171:## 3. XtdbStorageAdapter (packages/xtdb/src)
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:173:### 3.1 Physical tables
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:179:| `tx_assertions` | `XtdbStorageAdapter.ts:627` | `JSON([scopeKey, row.id])` (`:223`) | `scope_key` + the 20 `assertionColumns` (`codecs.ts:9-30`) + `value_identity` | Canonical ledger. One row per assertion. A retraction re-inserts the same `_id` with `retracted_at/_position/_tx_id` set. `value_identity` = canonical JSON of the typed value (used by constraints). |
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:184:| `tx_constraint_graphs`, `tx_constraint_generations` | `:639-642` | per run | graph copy of assertion columns; `run_id, source_k` | Scratch for `inline`/`projection` constraint strategies (`ConstraintValidation.ts:225-245`). |
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:190:### 3.2 One Triplex transact is one XTDB transaction
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:201:  ASSERT NOT EXISTS (tx_assertions WHERE id IN (new ids)) 'triplex-assertion-identity-conflict'  :209-213
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:208:Every INSERT sets `_valid_from = 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z` (`:38`) so a re-insert replaces the whole native valid lifetime. Triplex business time stays in the `valid_from/valid_to` columns; XTDB native valid time is not used. Triplex `recorded_at` is the Triplex clock, not XTDB system time.
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:212:### 3.3 Position allocation
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:219:### 3.4 Command-claim uniqueness
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:223:- The error mapping at `:292-298` treats `triplex-cas-conflict` and `triplex-command-conflict` as `XtdbSerializationConflict` (retried when `replaySafe`); the retry then finds the winning claim and reports `CommandAlreadyCommittedError`. `triplex-operation-duplicate` and `triplex-assertion-identity-conflict` become a plain `WriteError`.
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:225:### 3.5 CAS preconditions and write isolation
