lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:268:## 4. QleverStorageAdapter (packages/qlever/src)
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:270:### 4.1 Physical graph layout
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:283:### 4.2 Triples per assertion
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:291:| string / ref / json / blob, no `valid_to`, no `created_by` | **27** | 4 summary (`_row` JSON blob, `scalar_family`, `scalar_lexical`, `scalar_order`) + 5 value/identity (`id, entity_id, attribute, value_type, value_string`) + 4 each for `recorded_at, recorded_position, valid_from, schema_version` (value, `_order`, `_exact`, `_native`) + `entity_type` + `tx_id`. |
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:319:### 4.3 Writes: one conditional UPDATE, no engine transaction
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:332:      FILTER NOT EXISTS { VALUES ?n {new ids} GRAPH g { ?n field:id ?x } }         :224-227  identity reuse
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:339:If any guard fails the WHERE yields no rows and the UPDATE inserts nothing, so "all or nothing" holds for guard failures. The engine provides no rollback for execution errors: `packages/qlever/README.md` ("`--persist-updates` writes the complete native delta snapshot...") records that source review found unpublished delta mutation before persistence without exception rollback, and that a live counterexample showed a failed multi-operation request retaining its first INSERT. The adapter therefore uses one MODIFY, and failure atomicity stays unqualified.
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:341:### 4.4 Positions, claims, outcome reconciliation
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:351:| Reconcile after UPDATE | Poll `SELECT ?attempt` for the operation marker every 25 ms up to `resolutionTimeoutMs` (30 s). Marker present: committed. Marker absent but UPDATE acknowledged: re-read the position; if it differs from `sourceK` raise `QleverSerializationConflict`, else raise `WriteError` (a claim or identity guard rejected it). UPDATE errored or timed out and no marker by the deadline: `TransactionOutcomeUnknown`. | `:231-277` |
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:354:### 4.5 Managed writer
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:356:The "managed writer" is **not wired into the adapter**. It is a private Python experiment in `experiments/qlever-managed-writer/` (`broker.py` 347 lines, `native_worker.py` 212, `native_faults.py` 419, `DESIGN.md`, `NATIVE-PACKET.md`). Its design admits one prepared MODIFY at a time across all scopes under an `fcntl.flock` global lock, keeps an append-only hash-chained intent journal, and after any uncertain response terminates the owned server, fsyncs the persisted snapshot, restarts and verifies the marker. `README.md` states "No native trial has run" and goal 7 (atomic writes and recovery) is open. Offline tests: `python3 experiments/qlever-managed-writer/run_tests.py` (writes to `.qlever/managed-model/`, so not run here).
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:358:### 4.6 Restart and persistence
lab/research/R4-codebase-harness-map.md:361:- First start builds an index from a one-triple bootstrap file (`qlever-start.sh:4-8`). Later starts reuse `.qlever/data/triplex.index.*` plus the persisted updates file.
