    83	### 1.4 Evidence: memory per delta triple
    84	
    85	- **Structure** [S]: a `LocatedTriple` is a block index (8 B), an `IdTriple<0>` (4 Ids = 32 B) and a flag, 48 B with padding (`src/index/LocatedTriples.h:78-93 @ 6c5861a`). It is stored once per permutation (6), plus a hash set of inserted/deleted triples (`src/index/DeltaTriples.h:160-172 @ 6c5861a`), plus a **second deep copy** for the published snapshot. Terms not in the index vocabulary go to a local vocabulary (heap strings). Lower bound: 288 B per triple for the six copies, roughly doubled during the update.
    86	- **Measured** [P] (container RSS, baseline server 31 to 43 MB):
    87	
    88	| Scenario | Delta triples | RSS | Per delta triple |
    89	|----------|--------------|-----|------------------|
    90	| `INSERT ... WHERE` cross join, terms reused | 2.25M | 1,426 MB | ~0.61 KB |
    91	| After restart, replay of the persisted file | 4.5M | 1.87 GB | ~0.41 KB |
    92	| 40 x `INSERT DATA` of 25k triples, each triple with a new subject IRI and a new literal | 1.0M | 1,294 MB (peak 1,564 MB) | ~1.2 to 1.5 KB |
