    26	## 1. Schema model
    27	
    28	### 1.1 Answer in four lines
    29	
    30	- **Runtime shape.** An `EntityType` is a plain object holding `entityType` (PascalCase name), `schema` (a `TypeExpr.Struct` keyed by attribute), `attributes` (per-property handles) and `constraints`. It compiles to a content-addressed `ConfigNode` of kind `"entity-schema"`.
    31	- **Adapters cannot see it.** `StorageAdapterService` has no schema or config parameter. The only schema trace an adapter receives is the optional string `entityType` on each `TripleInput`, plus a constant `schema_version: 1` that both adapters hard-code.
    32	- **The schema lives in the same backend, as facts.** `ConfigStore` writes every config object, type, revision, snapshot and ref as ordinary assertions through `Triples`, in the reserved namespace `_triplex/config/`, with entity types `triplex.config-*`. A native query can therefore read the active release from the same `facts()` relation it uses for data.
    33	- **Neither native layer reads it today.** Native providers take attribute keys (XTDB) or `{key, type}` pairs (QLever) from `Attribute`/`EntityType` handles in the caller's process. Nothing in `packages/xtdb/src/native` or `packages/qlever/src/native` consults `ConfigStore`.
    34	
    35	### 1.2 The model, with citations
    36	
    37	| Concept | Where | Runtime representation |
    38	| --- | --- | --- |
    39	| Attribute definition | `packages/core/src/config/Attribute.ts:26-37` | `{_tag:"Attribute", key, type: TypeExpr, node: Effect<ConfigNode>, encode}`. Key must match `^:[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*\/[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*$` (`Attribute.ts:13`, check at `:62-69`). |
    40	| Attribute constructors | `Attribute.ts:93-131` | `text, number, integer, int64, boolean, date, instant, enumOf, ref(key, {entityType})`. `ref` records a `references-entity-type` ref to kind `entity-schema` (`:121-131`). No JSON or blob constructor exists. |
    41	| Attribute use | `Attribute.ts:39-52, 134-140` | `{required=false, cardinality="one", unique=false}`. Requiredness and cardinality belong to the entity's use, not the global attribute. |
    42	| Assertion descriptor | `Attribute.ts:142-155` | `{attribute, value: TripleValue, validFrom?}`. It carries no `entityType`. The caller adds `entityType` when building the `TransactOp`. |
    43	| EntityType | `packages/core/src/config/EntityType.ts:41-61` (type), `:69-154` (`make`) | See 1.3. |
    44	| TypeExpr | `packages/core/src/config/TypeExpr.ts:50-121` | Closed algebra: `Any, Prim(text\|number\|integer\|int64\|boolean\|date\|instant), Enum, Ref(kind), List, Struct(fields{type,optional,fallback}), Union, Constrained(base, constraints)`. Each constructor carries `v: 1`. |
    45	| TypeSchema | `packages/core/src/config/TypeSchema.ts:80-153` (`go`), `:162-163` (`compile`) | Compiles `TypeExpr` to an Effect `Schema.Codec<unknown, unknown>`. `int64` decodes the tagged `IntegerValue` (`:41-42`), not a JS number. |
    46	| ConfigNode | `packages/core/src/config/ConfigNode.ts:65` (interface), `:305` (`walk`) | `{kind, key, attrs, children[{rel,node}], refs[{rel,kind,key}], cid, type?}`. Children are hashed into the parent's `cid`; refs are not. |
    47	| ConfigStore | `packages/core/src/config/ConfigStore.ts:103-136` (service), `:195` (`load`), `:334` (`commit`), `:446` (`setRef`), `:495` (`layer`) | `load()` returns an `InMemoryConfigStore`; `resolveRef(name)` returns a `ConfigSnapshot` whose `root` is the full `ConfigNode` tree (`InMemoryConfigStore.ts:89-98`). |
    48	| Reserved storage names | `ConfigStore.ts:40-61` | Entity types `triplex.config-object/-type/-logical-object/-revision/-snapshot/-ref`. Attributes `:triplex/config-data` (JSON body), `:triplex/content-id`, `:triplex/config-kind`, `:triplex/config-key`, `:triplex/valid-under`, `:triplex/depends-on`, `:triplex/ref-target`. Entity ids prefixed `_triplex/config/`. |
