    76	### 1.4 Can an adapter or native layer reach the active schema?
    77	
    78	| Route | Works today? | Detail |
    79	| --- | --- | --- |
    80	| Via the `StorageAdapter` interface | No | No config handle in `StorageAdapterService` (`packages/core/src/storage/StorageAdapter.ts:21-89`). The adapter would need a factory option (for example `makeXtdbStorageAdapter(client, scope, {schema})`). `ConfigStore` sits above the adapter and writes through it, so an adapter-internal `ConfigStore.load()` per transaction would be circular and expensive. Passing the in-process `EntityType` objects into the adapter factory avoids both. |
    81	| Via `entityType` on assertions | Yes, as a label only | `TripleInput.entityType` is optional (`packages/core/src/Triple.ts:8-16`). It lands in the indexed `entity_type` column (XTDB `codecs.ts:27`, QLever `rdf.ts:22`). Nothing validates it against a schema at write time. Validation is a separate pass (`EntityValidation.revalidate`). |
