   241	  (`XtdbStorageAdapter.ts:111-186`, `cutConditions` l.42-70); it never masks the columns it returns. Ordinary `Triples.history` is documented to retain the full lifetime (`TINY-XTDB-CONTRACT-v4.md`, citing `store/Triples.ts` 249-255); this is distinct from the native `ctx.history()` relation.
   242	- It is classified as failure of a **new** target, not a regression: the older raw-lifetime contract is preserved as compatibility evidence.
