   399	- **Smallest next experiment.** On a 100k-edge chain of depth 50, time `selectSqlWithReachability` end to end, count XTDB transactions per read, and capture `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` for the round `INSERT ... SELECT`. Add a probe for `INSERT ... SELECT * FROM (XTQL(...))`.
   400	
   401	### Goal 4. Completed absence and negation at coherent cuts
   402	
   403	- **Proven (inherited).** `NOT EXISTS` tasks 09, 12, 13 and the watermark-based absence task 10 pass in SQL on the fixed fixtures. Single-call paging at a returned basis (native-entry l.328-373).
   404	- **Missing.** XTQL negation (`(not (exists? ...))`) never run. No task-wide P (2.6), so multi-call absence tasks can mix cuts. The QLever correlated `NOT EXISTS` counterexamples (`wiki/problems/native-correlation.md`) have not been run against XTDB.
   405	- **Smallest next experiment.** Experiments 2 and 5 in section 5: pin P per task and test a real writer between calls; port the flat and nested correlated `NOT EXISTS` controls to XTDB in SQL and XTQL.
   406	
   407	### Goal 5. Aggregates, typed groups, empties, exact overflow
   408	
   409	- **Proven (inherited).** SQL `SUM/COUNT/MIN/MAX/GROUP BY` in 06, 07, 08, 10, 17, 20; empty sum via `COALESCE`; BIGINT extrema exact.
   410	- **Missing.** XTQL `aggregate`. Overflow (Goal 2). Typed group identity beyond string keys. Set versus pair versus witness distinctions only on the four-node DAG. No aggregate at scale.
   411	- **Smallest next experiment.** XTQL `aggregate` versions of 06, 07, 08 plus grouped-empty, tie-winner and empty-max controls (QLever's three passing and two failing shape controls, `native-correlation.md`), both languages.
   412	
   413	### Goal 6. Cancellation, deadlines, resource ownership, cleanup
   414	
   415	- **Proven (inherited).** One SQL abort at 100 ms on a `pg_sleep(2.0)` then healthy reuse with `maxConnections: 1`; `physicalReclamationQualified:false` (native-entry l.374-417). The client holds the connection until the driver query settles
   416	  (`XtdbClient.ts:207-217`). Pre-cancelled requests issue no statement (`native-query.test.ts`). Native16 control: no read errors, 6/6 writers.
   417	- **Missing.** Any engine-side drain observation (see `wiki/problems/cancellation-observation-levels.md`: settled Effect, transport cancel, drained work and idle engine are four different claims). XTQL cancellation. Cancellation during a reachability round, where scratch rows
   418	  stay behind and `NativeWorkingOutcomeUnknown` retains them. 128 RPS dispatch arms failed availability and writer liveness and stay failures. Native 256-open had no visible writer inside 5 s.
   419	- **Smallest next experiment.** Experiment 9: abort a genuinely long XTQL and SQL scan, then read XTDB metrics/logs for the statement, and reuse the connection; repeat mid-reachability and count leftover `tx_native_relations` rows.
   420	
   421	### Goal 7. Atomic writes, receipts, migration, recovery
   422	
   423	- **Proven (inherited, shared).** Safe and unsafe CAS rejection (`P0004`) with rollback, claims, receipts (handoff review). Tiny v4: seven ACKs, five claims, seven operation receipts, Required rejection with no residue, two ConfigStore releases.
   424	  `resolveXtdbOperation` for unknown outcomes. Clean stopped backup/restore script only (`packages/xtdb/experiments/recovery.mjs`, no retained result here).
   425	- **Missing.** Abrupt crash or lost-ACK proof ("normal deterministic CAS competition is not crash/lost-ACK fault proof", handoff review). Engine restart with native reads at old cuts. Migration of existing data. For native: scratch-table residue after a crash mid-round.
   426	- **Smallest next experiment.** Experiment 10: kill the XTDB container mid-`COMMIT SYNC` and mid-reachability, restart, resolve the operation, re-read old cuts natively, inventory leftover scratch.
   427	
   428	### Goal 8. Bounded reuse, transactional publication, maintained supports
   429	
   430	- **Proven.** Nothing for native. Reachability scratch is erased after every read (`Reachability.ts:139-155`), so there is no reuse. `MaintainedQueries.ts` is a shared-package feature with no native consumer.
   431	- **Missing.** Cached closure keyed by scope, P, R, V and relation definition hash; cost of rebuild versus reuse; incremental alternate-support counting beyond the length-3 bound.
   432	- **Smallest next experiment.** Fold into experiment 7 (scale ramp): record transactions and wall time per reachability read at 100k edges. If one read costs tens of seconds, prototype reuse at the same P.
   433	
   434	### Goal 9. Bitemporal intervals, presence, corrections, lineage, deletion, cascades
   435	
   436	- **Proven (inherited).** Tiny v4 passes membership, lineage, history, corrections, presence/type-version facts, receipts on ordinary reads (47/52). Native: fractional-V half-open boundaries in XTQL, retirement masking in SQL, interval union (18), lineage (16), per-example two-time join (19).
   437	- **Missing.** The five target failures (3.1). XTQL retirement masking. Native reads of the configured fixture. Deletion and cascades (presence=false is an application convention with no cascade; `presence-reference-deletion-requirements-v1`). Same-timestamp distinct commits through native.
   438	  A mapping from R or P to system time (3.4).
   439	- **Smallest next experiment.** Experiment 1.
   440	
   441	### Goal 10. Public TypeScript and schema integration, scope, cursors, lifecycle, capabilities, consumers
   442	
   443	- **Proven (inherited).** 13 native-entry checks; `public-native-consumer-v2` (13-tarball clean consumer, typed native reads current and reopen; terminal absent here). Basis reports scope, P, V, R.
   444	- **Missing.** Contracts derived from schemas. Capability advertisement (runtime uses `Capabilities.none`). A cursor API (paging is hand-authored `OFFSET` on a first-page basis, O(offset) at scale). Scope isolation relies on authors using `ctx.facts()`.
   445	  Lifecycle: `openNative` builds a separate client with the default 20-connection pool. String ordering extension: pinned XTDB compares UTF-8 as unsigned bytes for `<` and `ORDER BY` (`expression.clj:803-806`, `expression/comparator.clj:62-66 @ c6c1962`), which is codepoint order, so a pass is expected but nobody has run it
   446	  (`wiki/research.md` says DuckDB/XTDB still need the ASCII extension run).
   447	- **Smallest next experiment.** Experiment 1 for the public helper, plus a mixed-case `ORDER BY`/range/page check (inside experiment 5).
