codex
H-X-CUT has a concrete counterexample already documented in R6 and present in the adapter: one XTDB transaction can contain several Triplex positions, but it writes only the final `tx_meta` position. System time alone cannot distinguish those intermediate cuts. The QLever research also shows that even one failed update can leave inconsistent permutations, which a watermark does not repair.
