   472	
   473	| Script | Question | Purpose |
   474	| --- | --- | --- |
   475	| `p1.mjs`, `p1b.mjs`, `p1c.mjs` | Q1 | `SYSTEM_TIME` syntax, equality, microseconds, abort behaviour, far-future time |
   476	| `p2.mjs`, `p2b.mjs`, `p10.mjs`, `p12.mjs` | Q2 | valid-time DML, retraction patterns, identical re-insert, timestamp bounds |
   477	| `p3a.mjs`, `p3b.mjs`, `p3c.mjs`, `p3d.mjs`, `p3e.mjs` | Q3 | types and OIDs, identifier handling |
   478	| `p8c.mjs`, `rawcopy.mjs`, `p9.mjs`, `p9b.mjs` | Q2, Q3, Q7 | COPY, transit parameters, wide rows, array parameters |
   479	| `p4.mjs`, `p13.mjs` | Q4 | XTQL operators, window functions, embedding forms |
   480	| `p5.mjs` | Q5 | temporal reads and basis |
   478	## Open questions needing experiments
   479	
   480	1. **Delta ceiling at scale.** What does a 1M-triple delta cost on a 100M-fact P+C index, per request (tiny update, 1k-triple update, 25k-triple update), and is the ~0.9 s fixed cost really O(delta) for single-triple requests? Direct measurement of tiny-update latency vs delta size was not done (inferred from the timing breakdown).
   481	2. **Update-error recovery.** After a timeout mid-mutation, does `rebuild-index` copy the partial permutations into the new index? Does a restart always clear the junk, and is there any case where junk is persisted? Does the 429 on a timed-out single operation always indicate partial application, or only after located triples were added?
   482	3. **Concurrency.** Query latency during a rebuild and during sustained updates on the 6-CPU VM, and whether updates that arrive during a rebuild are all carried over (source says yes, not exercised).
   483	4. **Mixed vocabulary order.** ORDER BY and FILTER ranges when half the strings are in the index vocabulary and half are local. Source says one comparator; not probed.
   484	5. **`US_POSIX` for non-ASCII.** Whether the repo's text (user names, free text) is ASCII-only enough for the `en_US_POSIX` build to act as a binary order, or whether a `QLEVER_NO_UNICODE` custom build is warranted. Also check `ignore-punctuation` choice against raw-SPARQL expectations.
   485	6. **Greedy planning quality.** Effect of `query-planning-budget=1` on the repo's 142-task packet and on realistic join-heavy reads over the 100M-fact P+C index.
   486	7. **Real latency at 100M facts on 6 CPU, 12 GiB.** Cold and warm latency for entity lookup, attribute range scan, GROUP BY and `ORDER BY ... LIMIT` on a 17 GB index with 12 GiB RAM; startup RSS for a multi-GB vocabulary; `--no-patterns` cost for predicate-count queries at that size.
   487	8. **Deep OFFSET paging cost and cache behavior** (does the sorted subtree stay in the cache across pages) on a million-row ordered result.
   488	9. **Durability.** Power-loss behavior of `<base>.update-triples` (no fsync found), and whether a crash during the temp-file write can leave `.update-triples.tmp` plus a stale file in a way that loses the last acknowledged update.
   489	10. **Upgrade path.** Which of #3190 (EXISTS planning), #3722 (planner memory accounting), #3306 (run-time memory limit), #3602 and #3678 (MINUS fixes) land in the next release, and whether to build a pinned master image once they matter.
